<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo noupdate="1">

    <!--
        Adds Production to the Cost Centre plan created by somgreen_config.

        This is what turns "we packed 4,000 cartons" into "we packed 4,000
        cartons at this conversion cost". Packing cost can then be read
        separately from the cost of selling and the cost of administering - and
        separately from the trading operation, which carries no conversion cost
        at all.

        CREATING THIS ACCOUNT ROUTES NOTHING TO IT. Work-center time does not
        post here by virtue of the account existing. mrp_account's
        _create_or_update_analytic_entry_for_record creates analytic lines only
        when the work center carries an analytic_distribution:

            if self.workcenter_id.analytic_distribution or ...

        So the Packing Line's Analytic Distribution must be pointed at this
        account in the UI, or it stays empty forever. That field cannot be set
        from a data file - it is JSON keyed by analytic account database id. See
        the note in mrp_workcenter.xml.

        Analytic is the SECOND line of defence, not the first. The factory cost
        split that the P&L depends on lives in the general ledger, in accounts
        503100-503900, because somgreen_account_reports groups its lines by
        account_type and never by analytic. Use this plan for the long tail of
        departmental spend, not for the recurring factory costs.
    -->

    <record id="analytic_production" model="account.analytic.account">
        <field name="name">Production</field>
        <field name="plan_id" ref="somgreen_config.analytic_plan_cost_centre"/>
    </record>

</odoo>
